Get from zero to a working API call in under five minutes. By the end of this guide you will have fetched a list of workspaces, identified a funnel ID, and retrieved contacts from that funnel.

## Prerequisites[​](#prerequisites "Direct link to Prerequisites")

- A Perspective account with Admin access
- An API key — see [API Keys](/perspective-docs-test/getting-started/api-keys) for how to create one

***

## Step 1 — Get your API key[​](#step-1--get-your-api-key "Direct link to Step 1 — Get your API key")

Every request must carry your API key in the `x-perspective-api-key` header. If you haven't created one yet, head to [API Keys](/perspective-docs-test/getting-started/api-keys) first, then come back.

Store the key in an environment variable so you don't hard-code it:

```
export PERSPECTIVE_API_KEY="your-api-key-here"
```

***

## Step 2 — Discover your workspaces and funnel IDs[​](#step-2--discover-your-workspaces-and-funnel-ids "Direct link to Step 2 — Discover your workspaces and funnel IDs")

Call `GET /v1/workspaces`. The response lists every workspace you have access to, and each workspace contains its campaigns (funnels). You'll use a `campaign.id` as the `funnelId` in subsequent calls.

- cURL
- JavaScript

```
curl https://perspective-api.co/v1/workspaces \

  -H "x-perspective-api-key: $PERSPECTIVE_API_KEY"
```

```
const response = await fetch('https://perspective-api.co/v1/workspaces', {

  headers: {

    'x-perspective-api-key': process.env.PERSPECTIVE_API_KEY,

  },

});

const { data } = await response.json();

console.log(data); // array of workspace objects
```

**Example response:**

```
{

  "data": [

    {

      "id": "ws_abc123",

      "name": "My Workspace",

      "campaigns": [

        { "id": "fnl_xyz789", "name": "Lead Capture Funnel", "status": "online" },

        { "id": "fnl_def456", "name": "Webinar Signup", "status": "offline" }

      ]

    }

  ]

}
```

Note the `id` value inside a `campaigns` entry — that is your `funnelId`.

***

## Step 3 — Fetch contacts for a funnel[​](#step-3--fetch-contacts-for-a-funnel "Direct link to Step 3 — Fetch contacts for a funnel")

Use the `funnelId` from Step 2 to call `GET /v1/funnels/{funnelId}/contacts`. The response is paginated (page 0 by default, up to 50 contacts per page).

- cURL
- JavaScript

```
curl "https://perspective-api.co/v1/funnels/fnl_xyz789/contacts?limit=10" \

  -H "x-perspective-api-key: $PERSPECTIVE_API_KEY"
```

```
const funnelId = 'fnl_xyz789';

const response = await fetch(

  `https://perspective-api.co/v1/funnels/${funnelId}/contacts?limit=10`,

  {

    headers: {

      'x-perspective-api-key': process.env.PERSPECTIVE_API_KEY,

    },

  }

);

const { data, meta } = await response.json();

console.log(`Fetched ${data.length} of ${meta.total} contacts`);
```

**Example response:**

```
{

  "data": [

    {

      "id": "cnt_111",

      "email": "alice@example.com",

      "firstName": "Alice",

      "status": "converted"

    }

  ],

  "meta": {

    "total": 342,

    "page": 0,

    "limit": 10,

    "hasNext": true

  }

}
```

If `meta.hasNext` is `true`, increment `page` and repeat until it is `false`. See [Pagination](/perspective-docs-test/getting-started/pagination) for a full loop example.

